  "facts": [
    "Baguashan Tunnel, spanning 4,928 meters westbound and 4,935 meters eastbound, opened on 29 April 2005, instantly cutting travel time between Changhua and Nantou by connecting Lincuo IC and Zhongxing JCT.",
    "On 5 October 2000, a collapsed civil house halted construction for a year, yet the tunnel resumed and opened to small vehicles before expanding to buses on 1 January 2006 and trucks on 1 January 2007.",
    "The tunnel’s 80 km/h speed limit and dual two‑lane tubes earned it the title of Taiwan’s longest highway tunnel upon opening, a record later surpassed by Hsuehshan Tunnel in 2006."
